WEBVTT

00:00:07.737 --> 00:00:12.737
DARRELL: McQueen is fading.
McQueen is fading. Fading fast.

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:17.217
(PANTING)

00:00:18.257 --> 00:00:20.017
CRUZ: Whoo-hoo! Yes!

00:00:20.097 --> 00:00:21.137
Ah! (CACKLES)

00:00:22.257 --> 00:00:25.497
Whoo! Did you see that? That was--

00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:33.337
Uh...

00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:35.857
Sorry. I didn't mean to--

00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:43.777
Hey, uh, boss, it's time to hit the road.

00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:47.017
Yeah.

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:49.017
(STAMMERING)

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:52.857
I want to thank everyone for the training.

00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:56.857
We better get going to Florida.

00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:09.457
CUTLASS: Welcome to
racing's greatest day!

00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:12.537
We're beach-side
at the Florida International Speedway...

00:01:12.737 --> 00:01:15.057
to kick off a new season
of Piston Cup racing.

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:16.937
It's the Florida 500.

00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:18.937
DARRELL: Forty-three cars
and a quarter million fans

00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:20.577
await today's intense contest of...

00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:22.737
strategy, skill, but most of all, speed.

00:01:23.057 --> 00:01:25.057
This crowd is in for
one great day of racing.

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:26.337
CUTLASS: I'm Bob Cutlass,

00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:28.217
joined as always
by my broadcasting partner...

00:01:28.777 --> 00:01:32.257
Darrell Cartrip and stat
sensation Natalie Certain.

00:01:32.297 --> 00:01:33.777
I've never seen
the numbers line up for Storm

00:01:33.857 --> 00:01:34.977
like they do today, Bob.

00:01:35.057 --> 00:01:38.937
Storm should be 96.8% unstoppable.

00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:40.377
DARRELL: Well, don't
overlook Lightning McQueen.

00:01:40.577 --> 00:01:41.737
Whipplefilter! Yeah-hoo!

00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.177
(ALL CHEERING)

00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:45.257
CUTLASS: We've heard stories
of the unusual way

00:01:45.297 --> 00:01:46.577
McQueen trained to get here.

00:01:47.457 --> 00:01:49.657
Now the question is did it work?

00:01:58.137 --> 00:02:03.697
Speed. I am... speed?

00:02:07.497 --> 00:02:08.777
(BANGING ON DOOR)

00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:10.617
MACK: Hey, boss, they're, uh...

00:02:10.657 --> 00:02:12.617
calling the racers to the track.

00:02:12.777 --> 00:02:13.977
(EXHALES)

00:02:15.857 --> 00:02:18.017
REPORTER: Jeff Gorvette,
how does today's talent stack up?

00:02:18.097 --> 00:02:19.457
Oh, I think we're in for a treat today.

00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:20.617
These racers are--

00:02:20.657 --> 00:02:23.457
Oh-- Hey, McQueen,
win one for us old guys.

00:02:23.497 --> 00:02:25.297
Hah! Will do, Jeff.

00:02:25.337 --> 00:02:27.337
-MATER: Hey, there, buddy!
-Hey, guys.

00:02:27.777 --> 00:02:30.497
-Stickers.
-Hey, Sal.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.137
-You okay?
-Yeah. Absolutely.

00:02:35.337 --> 00:02:37.617
Listen, you're gonna do great today.

00:02:37.697 --> 00:02:39.377
And no matter what happens...

00:02:39.457 --> 00:02:42.137
I'm going to move onto the next rookie
and forget I ever knew you.

00:02:42.177 --> 00:02:44.097
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

00:02:44.137 --> 00:02:45.457
I'm glad you're here.

00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:50.417
(CHUCKLING) Oh, wow! Nice costume.
Come here, let's get a picture.

00:02:50.497 --> 00:02:52.657
It's so great to meet my number-one fan.

00:02:53.057 --> 00:02:54.497
(SIGHS) What a jerk.

00:02:54.577 --> 00:02:57.577
-She's not a fan, Storm.
-Oh, hey there, champ.

00:02:57.657 --> 00:02:59.937
I heard you're selling
mudflaps after today.

00:02:59.977 --> 00:03:01.137
Is that true?

00:03:01.177 --> 00:03:03.537
Hey, you put me down
for the first case, okay?

00:03:06.577 --> 00:03:08.177
(ALL CHEERING)

00:03:13.337 --> 00:03:18.657
Lightning! Lightning McQueen!

00:03:19.697 --> 00:03:20.937
STERLING: Hey, Lightning!

00:03:21.497 --> 00:03:22.737
Hey, Mr. Sterling.

00:03:23.377 --> 00:03:24.937
To the future, eh, champ?

00:03:25.457 --> 00:03:27.537
Yeah. To the future.

00:03:28.537 --> 00:03:31.777
Hey, just focus on
what you're here to do, kid.

00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:33.577
Thanks, Smokey.

00:03:33.737 --> 00:03:35.897
SMOKEY: Now, go make Hud proud.

00:03:36.057 --> 00:03:37.297
You got it.

00:03:37.697 --> 00:03:39.377
DARRELL: Boogity, boogity,
boogity, let's go racing!

00:03:48.537 --> 00:03:50.617
CUTLASS: McQueen
is making steady progress

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:51.857
in the early parts of this race.

00:03:52.377 --> 00:03:54.377
NATALIE CERTAIN: Well,
it won't be enough to catch Storm.

00:03:54.457 --> 00:03:55.537
DARRELL: Considering
he started dead last...

00:03:56.057 --> 00:03:57.897
I don't think
he's doing half-bad out there.

00:04:06.737 --> 00:04:08.857
SMOKEY: Not too shabby!

00:04:08.977 --> 00:04:10.737
You keep this up,
you'll finish in the top 10!

00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:12.697
Top 10's not gonna cut it, Smokey.

00:04:12.737 --> 00:04:14.137
I got to go all the way.

00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:16.897
So dig in! Remember your training.

00:04:17.057 --> 00:04:18.937
Find Storm and chase him down!

00:04:19.097 --> 00:04:20.857
Oh, tell him he has
three laps to catch me!

00:04:21.057 --> 00:04:23.417
Cruz says you've got
three laps to catch her.

00:04:23.577 --> 00:04:25.297
Yeah, okay! Tell her, thanks.

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:35.377
-Cruz, what are you doing here?
-Oh, Mr. Sterling, I was just--

00:04:35.537 --> 00:04:37.017
I'd like you to head back
to the training center right away.

00:04:37.097 --> 00:04:38.617
Oh. But why?

00:04:38.737 --> 00:04:41.097
I need you to get Kurt up to speed
for the race next weekend.

00:04:41.257 --> 00:04:43.777
Um... Wait, not Kurt.
He's the bug guy, right?

00:04:43.857 --> 00:04:45.097
The other one-- Ronald. Yes!

00:04:45.377 --> 00:04:46.897
But I want to stay and watch.

00:04:46.937 --> 00:04:48.657
That's not gonna happen, Cruz.

00:04:48.857 --> 00:04:49.937
Now go.

00:04:50.097 --> 00:04:52.057
(STUTTERS) But Mr. McQueen
still has a chance--

00:04:52.217 --> 00:04:53.577
Just go do your job!

00:04:54.137 --> 00:04:55.257
Yes, sir.

00:04:55.697 --> 00:04:57.777
And take off that spoiler
and those racing tires.

00:04:57.817 --> 00:04:58.937
You look ridiculous!

00:04:59.017 --> 00:05:02.697
You are a trainer, remember?
Not a racer! (ECHOING)

00:05:04.457 --> 00:05:05.617
McQUEEN: If you were a racer,

00:05:05.657 --> 00:05:08.177
you'd know what
I'm talking about but you're not!

00:05:08.257 --> 00:05:09.457
So you don't!

00:05:13.577 --> 00:05:15.857
STERLING: No. (LAUGHS)
She's not a racer. She's a trainer.

00:05:21.257 --> 00:05:22.817
(CRUZ WHOOPING)

00:05:24.497 --> 00:05:27.017
CRUZ: I've wanted to become
a racer forever!

00:05:27.177 --> 00:05:28.577
Because of you!

00:05:31.977 --> 00:05:35.577
It was my one shot and I didn't take it.

00:05:35.737 --> 00:05:39.497
It was my one shot and I didn't take it.

00:05:42.777 --> 00:05:43.697
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:05:43.857 --> 00:05:44.777
SMOKEY: Wreck in two.
Wreck in turn two.

00:05:44.817 --> 00:05:45.897
Go low. Go low.

00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:50.217
(McQUEEN GRUNTS)

